  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="paper-hero-title">
      <div class="hero-art"><img src="assets/paper-crimson/knot-paper-light.svg" width="520" height="370" alt="An intricate engraved knot: separate threads forming one connected structure."><span class="art-caption">CONNECTED KNOWLEDGE / SHARED CONTEXT</span></div>
      <h1 id="paper-hero-title">An open<br>company brain.</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">Knowledge and work, connected.<br>A shared context for people and AI agents.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#model">Explore the model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="incident-walkthrough.html">Follow an incident <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <dl class="facts"><div><dt>454<span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></dt><dd>REFERENCE RECORDS</dd></div><div><dt data-search-entry-count>0<span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></dt><dd>SEARCHABLE ENTRIES</dd></div><div><dt>Open</dt><dd>SOURCE &amp; KNOWLEDGE</dd></div><div><dt>In progress</dt><dd>PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT</dd></div></dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section demo-section" id="model" aria-labelledby="model-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">01 / SEE THE CONNECTIONS</span><h2 id="model-title">One incident.<br>The whole picture.</h2><p>A requirement, an attempted export, its evidence and the decision that follows. See how the parts connect.</p></div>
      <div class="workbench">
        <div class="workbench-header"><span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> NORTHSTAR / INCIDENT WALKTHROUGH</span><span class="tag">ILLUSTRATIVE CASE</span></div>
        <div class="demo-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Inspect the incident"><button role="tab" id="tab-meaning" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="demo-panel" data-stage="meaning">01 Meaning</button><button role="tab" id="tab-work" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" aria-controls="demo-panel" data-stage="work">02 Work</button><button role="tab" id="tab-evidence" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" aria-controls="demo-panel" data-stage="evidence">03 Evidence</button><button role="tab" id="tab-decision" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" aria-controls="demo-panel" data-stage="decision">04 Decision</button></div>
        <div class="demo-body">
          <div class="demo-answer" id="demo-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-meaning" tabindex="0"><div class="answer-meta"><span id="stage-type">DEFINITION</span><span class="tag" id="stage-number">01 / 04</span></div><h3 id="stage-title">Start with what<br>the work means.</h3><p id="stage-copy">Make the requirement and its terms explicit. The team and its agents need the same reference before they examine what happened.</p><a id="stage-link" class="inline-link" href="incident-walkthrough.html">Read the complete incident <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          <div class="connection-list" role="group" aria-label="Connected parts"><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT CONTEXT / CONNECTED RECORDS</p><ol><li data-record="meaning" class="active"><span class="record-index">01</span><span><strong>Meaning</strong><small>The terms and requirement</small></span><span class="record-state">SELECTED</span></li><li data-record="work"><span class="record-index">02</span><span><strong>Work</strong><small>The attempted export</small></span><span class="record-state">LINKED</span></li><li data-record="evidence"><span class="record-index">03</span><span><strong>Evidence</strong><small>What the examination found</small></span><span class="record-state">LINKED</span></li><li data-record="decision"><span class="record-index">04</span><span><strong>Decision</strong><small>What should happen next</small></span><span class="record-state">LINKED</span></li></ol></div>
        </div>
        <p class="workbench-note">A guided illustration of the existing example. No live agent or external service is running.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section system-section" id="system" aria-label="Session continuity illustration">
      <div class="split-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE COMPANY BRAIN</span><h2 id="system-title">The project remembers.<br>The agent continues.</h2></div><p>Sessions end. The knowledge behind the work should stay with the project, ready for the next person or agent.</p></div>
      <div class="system-flow" role="group" aria-label="A session records project knowledge and a later session recovers context"><div class="session-node"><span class="eyebrow">SESSION A</span><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><strong>Investigate<br>&amp; record</strong><small>Temporary session memory</small></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="project-node"><span class="eyebrow">SHARED PROJECT STATE</span><div class="state-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</div><strong>Continuing knowledge</strong><div class="state-tags"><span>Work</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Decisions</span></div></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="session-node"><span class="eyebrow">SESSION B</span><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><strong>Recover<br>&amp; continue</strong><small>Fresh context for the task</small></div></div>
      <p class="section-footnote">Context views select what a task needs. Permissions and freshness still apply.</p><p class="concept-introduction-link"><a class="inline-link" href="company-brain.html#company-knowledge">How the company brain works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section craft-section" id="paper-craft" aria-labelledby="paper-craft-title">
      <div class="split-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / SOFTWARE WORK</span><h2 id="paper-craft-title">Meet Craft.<br>Make the model explicit.</h2></div><p>Craft describes the concepts, rules and behavior an implementation must preserve. The Lab keeps the context around that work.</p></div>
      <div class="craft-grid"><article><div class="code-heading"><span>01 / CALCULATION</span><span aria-hidden="true">ƒ(x)</span></div><h3>Evaluate a request.</h3><p>A capacity check answers whether a request fits. It calculates a result without changing the state.</p><div class="code-line"><span>capacity.check</span><span>→ result</span></div></article><article><div class="code-heading"><span>02 / OPERATION</span><span aria-hidden="true">↦</span></div><h3>Change the state.</h3><p>Reserving that capacity performs a change. Its effects and constraints belong in the model.</p><div class="code-line"><span>capacity.reserve</span><span>→ effect</span></div></article></div>
      <div class="section-tail"><p>A conceptual example. Product and release work continues.</p><a class="inline-link" href="../craft-documentation-proposal/craft-model.html#definition">Read the Craft model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section explore-section" id="paper-explore" aria-labelledby="paper-explore-title"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">04 / GO A LITTLE DEEPER</span><h2 id="paper-explore-title">Find your way in.</h2><p>Follow a concrete example, inspect the model or go straight to an exact definition.</p></div><div class="destination-grid"><a href="start-here.html"><span class="eyebrow">BEGIN</span><h3>Get to know<br>the Lab.</h3><span class="destination-bottom">Start here <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a><a href="governance-lab-reference.html#system-map"><span class="eyebrow">EXPLORE</span><h3>See how the<br>parts connect.</h3><span class="destination-bottom">System map <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a><a href="lab-reference-library.html#catalog-definitions"><span class="eyebrow">LOOK UP</span><h3>Find an exact<br>reference.</h3><span class="destination-bottom">Reference library <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a></div></section>
  </main>

